### Color distribution

The visual treatment can be summarized as:

- 85–90% neutral UI: white, light gray, near-black typography.
- Primary blue: mainly action buttons, selected tabs, and emphasis.
- Indigo, pink, cyan: occasional status labels, feature icons, and metrics.
- Orange, coral, teal, purple gradients: reserved for creative showcases, product imagery, and the promotional banner.

The gradients are particularly important. They create visual energy behind product previews, while the actual interface remains clean and functional.

Replication rule: Keep the application interface neutral. Let visual content and a limited number of active controls provide the color.

## 3. Detailed layout breakdown

The original appears to be a desktop landing page scaled down into a tall screenshot. The following proportions are inferred, not exact measurements from the site's code.

| Section            | Layout composition          | Design details                                                                                                         |
| ------------------ | --------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Navigation         | Slim horizontal header      | Small logo left, compact navigation right, blue CTA. No heavy border or shadow.                                        |
| Hero               | Centered single-column      | Oversized two-line headline, blue second line, short supporting text, two compact CTAs.                                |
| Hero preview       | Large centered visual       | Approximately 85% of page width. White application window inside a colorful abstract frame.                            |
| Announcement       | Full-width horizontal strip | Coral/teal gradient background, brief white text, small blue CTA on the right.                                         |
| Feature showcase   | Asymmetric two-column       | Narrow text column on the left, large screenshot on the right. Repeated three times with substantial vertical spacing. |
| Product examples   | Tabs + editorial grid       | Light gray section, centered heading, understated tabs, descriptive copy, and a 2×2 image gallery.                     |
| Engagement models  | Three equal cards           | Flat light gray cards, subtle rounded corners, colored category labels, concise content.                               |
| Business outcomes  | Three-column metrics        | Explanatory text followed by two large indigo numbers, such as 3.4x and +18%.                                          |
| Platform updates   | Horizontal card collection  | Image-led white cards on light gray, rounded thumbnails, compact labels and descriptions.                              |
| Creative workflows | Asymmetric image gallery    | Centered heading, partner logos, and a six-image automotive gallery using mixed tile widths.                           |
| FAQ                | Split-column accordion      | Heading left; stacked white, rounded accordion cards on the right, all on light gray.                                  |

### What stands out about the composition

The design uses three recurring spatial patterns rather than many different layouts:

Centered introductions. Headlines and short supporting paragraphs are centered at the beginning of major sections. This creates a deliberate, calm rhythm.

Asymmetric feature presentations. The feature rows give roughly 30% of their content width to text and 60% to the screenshot, with the rest as separation. The screenshot dominates because the product is the evidence.

Structured collections. When several items must be displayed together, the design switches to equal-width cards, horizontal carousels, or a curated image grid.

That controlled repetition is a major reason the page feels cohesive.

## 4. Typography, spacing, and component styling

Typography contributes heavily to the reference's professional appearance. It relies on clean, modern sans-serif type with relatively light headline weights rather than heavy, bold text throughout.

### Recommended typography system

| Element         | Suggested specification         | Visual intention                    |
| --------------- | ------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |
| Font family     | Inter, Geist, or Helvetica Neue | Modern, neutral sans-serif          |
| Hero heading    | 64–72px, weight 400–500         | Large, elegant, uncluttered         |
| Section heading | 36–44px, weight 400–500         | Clear without becoming overpowering |
| Card heading    | 20–24px, weight 500–600         | Balanced hierarchy                  |
| Body text       | 15–16px, weight 400             | Readable and compact                |
| Small labels    | 12–14px, weight 500             | Quiet supporting information        |
| Display metrics | 56–72px, weight 300–400         | Large, refined emphasis             |

The hero uses tight line spacing, while supporting paragraphs have more relaxed line height. Text remains mostly left-aligned inside content sections, even though primary introductions are centered.

